 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbs: always at the end",
     "texto": [
      "The Japanese verb goes at the **end** of the sentence and **does not change with the person**: **たべます** is «I eat», «you eat», «he eats», «we eat»…",
      "The polite form ends in **ます** (pronounced «mas», almost without the u). It is used for the present and the future.",
      "To negate, **ます** changes to **ません**: **たべません** (I don't eat). To ask, add **か**: **たべます か**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "The -masu form",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Form",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Japanese",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "English",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "statement",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "たべます",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "I eat, I will eat",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "negative",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "たべません",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "I don't eat",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "question",
